findings.text:
§15's deliverable asserts "The written bytes and the rename semantics are unchanged" while naming only `_store.write_json_atomically` as the replacement; that writer's defaults serialise with `indent=2` and `mode=0o600`, so a literal call produces indented bytes and a 0o600 file, whereas the removed `run_paths._write_json_atomically` wrote compact bytes (`json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True) + "
"`) at the process default 0o644 — measured: run_paths b'{"project": "reckon", "renewed_at": 1760550000.5, "session": "f653840f"}
' mode 0o644 against _store b'{
  "project": "reckon",
  "renewed_at": 1760550000.5,
  "session": "f653840f"
}
' mode 0o600, not identical — and §15's done-when ("§8's tests … pass unchanged") cannot catch this, because those tests parse the JSON and are blind to indentation and mode.
